::Q01::Which Python module is used to delete files and directories?{
~shutil
=os
~file
~delete
}

::Q02::Which function should be used to delete a file in Python?{
=os.remove()
~os.rmdir()
~os.unlink_directory()
~os.delete()
}

::Q03::Which function should be used to delete an empty directory in Python?{
~os.remove()
~os.delete()
~os.clear()
=os.rmdir()
}

::Q04::[markdown] What is the purpose of `os.path.exists()` in the file-deletion example?{
~It permanently deletes the specified file
~It changes a file into a directory
~It checks whether a directory contains files
=It checks whether the specified file or directory exists before attempting deletion
}

::Q05::[markdown] What happens if `os.rmdir()` is used on a directory that contains files?{
~A PermissionError is raised
=An OSError is raised
~A FileNotFoundError is raised
~The directory and all its files are automatically deleted
}
